{"event":"result","result":{"conversation_id":"c34c3237-7c08-4c1e-b5ed-e833ae4e36c5","status":"SUCCESS","response":"Implemented fixes for the Intervals.icu integration:\n\n1. **Server (`server.py`)**\n   * Updated `current_user` to:\n     - Prefer the `Authorization` header.\n     - Fall back to a `token` query‑parameter (useful after the OAuth redirect).\n   * Revised `auth_init` to use this robust user detection and return proper 401 responses when no user is identified.\n\n2. **Frontend (`static/app.js`)**\n   * Modified the “Connect Intervals.icu” link to include the current client token as a query parameter (`?token=…`). This ensures the server can associate the request with the correct user without relying on the Authorization header.\n\nThese changes address the failing “Connect” button for all athletes and prevent the need for manual reconnection after an hour.  \n\nThe detailed root‑Implemented fixes for the Intervals.icu integration:\n\n1. **Server (`server.py`)**\n   * Updated `current_user` to:\n     - Prefer the `Authorization` header.\n     - Fall back to a `token` query‑parameter (useful after the OAuth redirect).\n   * Revised `auth_init` to use this robust user detection and return proper 401 responses when no user is identified.\n\n2. **Frontend (`static/app.js`)**\n   * Modified the “Connect Intervals.icu” link to include the current client token as a query parameter (`?token=…`). This ensures the server can associate the request with the correct user without relying on the Authorization header.\n\nThese changes address the failing “Connect” button for all athletes and prevent the need for manual reconnection after an hour.  \n\nThe detailed root‑cause analysis and reasoning are documented in **ANSWER.md** in the artifact directory.  \n\nYou can now re‑run the app and verify that the Connect flow works for all users.  \n\n\n\n---  \n\n\n\n**Next steps / verification**  \n- Start the server (`python3 server.py`) and open the UI.  \n- Click **Connect Intervals.icu**; the OAuth flow should complete and the status should show a connected athlete.  \n\n\n\nIf any further issues arise, let me know!  \n\n\n\n*(All changes were made within the current workspace as requested.)*\n","duration_seconds":248.536635,"num_turns":1,"usage":{"input_tokens":39434,"output_tokens":16034,"thinking_tokens":0,"cache_read_tokens":560704,"total_tokens":55468}}}
